  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "tokugawa-ieyasu-yamaoka-s336-p44450",
      "source_en": "“It is my belief that the gold may have been brought from the region around Ryukyu, where there are gold mines. They did not know where it had come from. When asked where they themselves were from, they merely said they were people of Kōrai. Kōrai is the same as Kōra—that is, what the people of the Great Ming call wokou.”",
